            <ArticleTitle>Successful coronary intervention for chronic total occlusion in an anomalous right coronary artery using the retrograde approach via a collateral vessel.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E1-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the first case in the literature of successful coronary intervention in a totally occluded anomalous right coronary artery originating from the left sinus of Valsalva using several techniques, including the retrograde approach via a collateral vessel, the anchoring technique and the five-in-six system.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
